# Frozen measurement code: SHA-256 of the nine files that produced the measured values and are not in the run-day manifest
#
# The measurement code of version 1.1.0 was frozen at commit 73b4cca16e7c (full id 73b4cca16e7c390e4ff487c0b3f0a65af1519c7f,
# 9 November 2026), before the Sepolia run of 12 November 2026. The files below are the code that issued, verified and timed
# the credentials, deployed the Sepolia setup, and set the compiler and the locked toolchain. The contract and the scripts
# that the run-day manifest covers are listed, with their hashes, in run_day/MANIFEST_SUBSET.sha256 and
# run_day/RUN_DAY_MANIFEST.sha256, so they are not repeated here.
#
# Each line: SHA-256, size in bytes, path. The hashes were computed on 22 November 2026 from the files as stored in the
# repository (the line endings of the commit, which are LF for these nine files), and each equals the SHA-256 of
# "git show 73b4cca16e7c:<path>". These files are unchanged in versions 1.1.0 and 1.1.1; package.json and
# package-lock.json therefore still give the version as 1.1.0.
#
# Check (bash, from the repository root):   sha256sum -c <(tr -d '\r' < FROZEN_CODE.sha256 | grep -v '^#' | awk '{print $1"  "$3}')
# Check one file against the commit (in a git clone):   git show 73b4cca16e7c:<path> | sha256sum
# A checkout made with core.autocrlf=true (the Git for Windows default) writes these files with CRLF endings, and then the first check fails; clone with git clone -c core.autocrlf=false, or use the second check.
#
